    "description": "A political-philosophical essay on Cuba analyzing the structural mechanism of totalitarian power, the trap of the political pendulum, the anthropological deformation caused by six decades of dictatorship, and proposing a concrete guide for democratic transition grounded in the republican ethics of José Martí.",
    "abstract": "This essay argues that Cuba's central problem is not who holds power but the form in which power exists. It analyzes how the totalitarian dictatorship built a mechanism of control that destroyed the economy, corrupted public morality, and anthropologically deformed society. It proposes concrete principles for a democratic transition that avoids the political pendulum trap, including an operational guide for the first 24 months: from the release of political prisoners to the demilitarization of the state and the first free elections. All grounded in the republican ethics of José Martí.",
